+    judged on both sides = NOT COMPARED (exit 3) -> verdict-sample.sh row "not run", vdone notrun (obligation pending,
+    streak and pool untouched); a judged-vs-judged difference is still a MISMATCH.
+(b) verdict-sample.sh: the reference run gets neither the job's --deadline nor its --budget, but its own --budget.
+(c) a reference exiting outside 0|1 or writing a partial record is renamed aside; findref never returns a partial.
+Review F1 (class: a caller of cloud-verdict-compare.py that reads exit 3 as "inputs differ"): cloud-late.py decides on the
+comparator's verdict line checked against its exit code (OUTCOMES); NOT COMPARED, a crash or a line/exit disagreement is
+"not made", never CLOUD_LATE_APPLY off nor POOL OFF (class CloudLate).
+DRI note 2026-11-17 (reviews/vs-ref-notrun-not-compared-dri-note-20261117.md): a cloud verdict the reference did not judge
+(reference NOT RUN or a timeout UNKNOWN) makes the comparison NOT COMPARED (exit 3; the sample stays pending), even when
+other pairs were judged on both sides; a mutant only the cloud did not judge stays not compared for that line only.
+Fixture: tools-local/fixtures/vsnr-p9-9ccbf3fd, a copy (SHA256SUMS) of cloud-jobs/tm-nightly-20261116T1607Z-p9-9ccbf3fd's
+job.json, cloud-verdicts.json, vm-ref.fin.json (the resumed reference: 2 of the cloud's 5 KILLED timed out) and
+vm-ref.partial-deadline-20261117T0534Z.json, read only and copied into a temp dir; nothing live is written. The VM run is
+the VS_TM stub hook of verdict-sample.sh.
+run: python3 -I tools-local/test_vs_ref_notrun.py [-v]            (the installed files: these tests FAIL there)
+     VSNR_SFX=.new-vsnr python3 -I tools-local/test_vs_ref_notrun.py  (the staged copies, <file><sfx> where present)"""
